"Alan died in his sleep at his back window that evening; it was quiet, and he felt nothing."
"Gramps, the voice who hands out Reincarnation Points, brought Alan's soul here as an experiment."
"The experiment is a soul set down grown, in a made body, with no birth and no childhood."
"Alan's soul had banked 5 Reincarnation Points from lives before; Gramps spent them on his behalf."
"Four points bought a dimensional affinity purer than the three-point grade anyone else has had."
"One Reincarnation Point was left unspent, and Gramps holds it for her still."
"The body was made for a soul named Nala who never came, so the System already knew her name."
"The first Nala chose a quiet rest over a new life, and her made body waited empty."
"The body is a woman's because it was shaped for that first Nala, not for Alan."
"Alan's soul was chosen for the body because both carried the same deep leaning toward space."
"The line too bright to read in her status is her Emblems, which show once she first casts."
"Her Emblems are [Experiment] and [Unique], as the gods mark a soul like hers."
"Gramps set her down at Millbrook because it is quiet and far from eyes that hunt for legacies."
"Gramps expects big things of her; a deed of real note earns her Legend Points."
"A native who learns she holds dimensional affinity may covet it, fear it, or seek to use her."
